// Committed mesh-integrity baselines, read by `level_check`.
//
// The check is relative: an error only when the count rises meaningfully above
// the figure recorded here. Re-commit these numbers when terrain generation or
// meshing changes on purpose. The count is per level *file*, not per segment
// definition: a segment instanced twice contributes twice.
//
// Every level reads **zero** open edges, and zero is the rule rather than a
// tolerance. `level_check` still permits a small absolute rise before it
// errors, so a rise recorded here is a real regression — read it as one.
//
// Two separate causes have been closed. The first was lattice coincidence: a
// sample landing exactly on an iso-surface, which `carve_with_sdf` encoded as a
// density of exactly zero. Debiasing the density writes fixed 218, 22 and 1174
// counts that had been attributed to three different bugs.
//
// The second was `subsidence`'s residual 26, and it was not a meshing failure
// at all — the surface was watertight to within an ULP. Two marching-cubes
// cells sharing a lattice edge disagreed about the vertex on it, in the last
// bit, for two reasons: the edge table handed them the endpoints in opposite
// orders, and the interpolation was written `a·(1 - t) + b·t`, which rounds
// even the components that are equal at both ends. Vertex matching snaps
// positions to a grid, so a sub-micron disagreement is invisible until it
// straddles a snapping boundary — which is why the count was small,
// scale-dependent, and immune to nudging authored surfaces off the lattice.
// Both are now pinned by tests in `marching_cubes.rs`.
//
(
    entries: [
        (level: "test_arena.level.ron", triangles: 193828, open_edges: 0),
        (level: "island_sea.level.ron", triangles: 195952, open_edges: 0),
        (level: "test_empty_terrain.level.ron", triangles: 100276, open_edges: 0),
        (level: "test_segments.level.ron", triangles: 224756, open_edges: 0),
        (level: "subsidence.level.ron", triangles: 301292, open_edges: 0),
        (level: "thin_ice.level.ron", triangles: 90524, open_edges: 0),
        (level: "wrecking_yard.level.ron", triangles: 120792, open_edges: 0),
        (level: "skyway.level.ron", triangles: 205916, open_edges: 0),
    ],
)
